# Real backend on the staging Odoo 18 instance (foom_fnb_api addon).
# Use with: npm run dev:staging   (or)   npm run build:staging
#
# Verified live on 2026-09-17 by calling GET /api/kds/tenant/config and
# GET /api/kds/companies directly against staging:
#   - the module is mounted, CORS is wide open (Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *)
#   - response shapes match docs/api-contract.md exactly, no frontend code
#     changes were needed beyond these env vars
#
# Two things to know about before relying on this in front of real staff:
#
# 1. tenant/config's logo_url currently comes back as a plain http:// URL
#    (http://odoo18-staging.foomid.id/logo.png?company=1) even though the
#    site itself is https. A page loaded over https will block that as
#    mixed content, so the outlet logo won't render until the backend sets
#    foom_fnb_api.public_base_url (or fixes web.base.url) to the https
#    origin — see System Parameters in Odoo. Not a frontend bug/fix.
#
# 2. VITE_WS_URL below is an UNVERIFIED GUESS. ws_gateway/kds_ws_gateway.py
#    is a separate process from the Odoo web server, and it isn't reachable
#    at any guessed path yet — wss://.../ws and wss://.../kds/ws both fail
#    the handshake (code 1006), and the gateway's default port (8765)
#    isn't open through Cloudflare either. Confirm the real gateway URL
#    with whoever deployed it and update this line. Until then this is
#    safe to ship as-is: KitchenSocket (src/ws/kitchenSocket.js) falls back
#    to 5s REST polling after 3 failed socket attempts, so the board still
#    works — just without instant push updates.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://odoo18-staging.foomid.id/api/kds
VITE_WS_URL=wss://odoo18-staging.foomid.id/ws
VITE_USE_MOCKS=false
